  "introduction": {
    "text": "Chiesa di San Giovanni a Porta Latina is a basilica church in Rome near the Porta Latina of the Aurelian Wall. It is historically significant for its association with the martyrdom of St John the Evangelist, its long architectural evolution from the 5th to the 20th centuries, and its role as a site of early same‑sex marriage.",
    "sourceIds": ["wikipedia"]
  },
